---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, POLICY_UPDATED } from "../../components/site-data";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy · Is There a Burn Ban?"
  description="What Is There a Burn Ban? collects (only what alerts need), what it never collects, and how to delete it."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <main id="content" class="page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Privacy</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Updated {POLICY_UPDATED}.</p>
    <p>
      You can check burn bans without an account. We only keep what we need to send the alerts you ask for.
      There are no ads, no tracking scripts and no cookies of our own, and we don't sell or rent anything about you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="location">Your location</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When you tap <em>Use my location</em>, your browser asks you first. If you allow it, the page rounds the
        position to four decimal places (about 10 meters) and sends it to our status lookup to find your county.
        A ZIP code you type is sent the same way.
      </li>
      <li>We use that query to answer and then drop it. We don't save it to a database.</li>
      <li>
        Your browser remembers the last place you picked (county name, and the ZIP or coordinates if you gave them) in
        its own local storage, so the page can show it next time. It stays on your device. Clear this site's data in your
        browser to remove it.
      </li>
      <li>The site doesn't guess your location from your IP address.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="email">Email alerts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If you sign up, on the site or through an AI assistant using our tools, we store your email address and the
        counties you picked.
      </li>
      <li>
        It's double opt-in: we send one confirmation email, and nothing else until you click the link in it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every alert has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing stops all email right away. We keep the address marked as
        unsubscribed so the link keeps working. Email us and we'll delete it completely.
      </li>
      <li>We send email through Resend, an email delivery service. It handles your address only to deliver our messages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="push">Push alerts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If you turn on alerts in your browser, the browser gives us a push subscription: a web address at your browser
        maker's push service (Google, Apple, Mozilla or Microsoft) plus encryption keys. We store that and the counties you
        picked. It doesn't include your name or email.
      </li>
      <li>Turning alerts off deletes it. We also delete it when the push service tells us it has expired.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="logs">Delivery records and usage counts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        For each alert we send, we log the county, the result and a masked target (for example the first letter of an email
        address), so we can fix delivery problems.
      </li>
      <li>
        We count requests to our API and MCP server: which endpoint or tool, the response status, the country, and a broad
        client type (browser, bot, AI agent or script). We don't store IP addresses, full browser details, or what you
        searched for.
      </li>
      <li>
        The site runs on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare handles IP addresses to deliver pages and block abuse.
        We don't keep request logs with IP addresses ourselves.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sharing">Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We share data only with the services above, and only to run the site and send alerts. We don't sell data or share it
      for advertising. We would disclose it only if the law required us to.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Questions or deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We'll delete your email signup or answer questions about
      your data. See also the <a href="/terms/">terms</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
